## Why This Is Asked
Tests end-to-end Azure AI design for a per-tenant, real-time risk pipeline, including data isolation, PII handling, and production-readiness at scale.

## Key Concepts
- Event-driven ingestion (Event Hubs) and scalable compute (Functions/ACIs)
- KB grounding (Cognitive Search) per tenant
- OpenAI integration with tenant-scoped prompts
- Per-tenant state (Cosmos DB) and secret management (Key Vault)
- PII redaction (Text Analytics) and Data Lake auditing
- Performance, latency, and testability at scale

## Code Example
```javascript
async function scoreEvent(event, tenantId) {
  // Fetch tenant-specific knowledge base
  const kb = await cognitiveSearch.search(tenantId, event.query);

  // Derive risk score with OpenAI
  const response = await openai.chat.completions.create({
    model: "gpt-4",
    messages: [{
      role: "system",
      content: `Tenant: ${tenantId}. KB: ${kb}. Score risk 0-100.`
    }, {
      role: "user", 
      content: event.data
    }]
  });

  // Store with tenant isolation
  await cosmosDB.createItem({
    tenantId,
    score: response.score,
    explanation: response.explanation,
    timestamp: new Date()
  });
}
```

## Why This Is Asked

This tests design for guardrails, data isolation, and cost controls in Azure OpenAI deployments, a common advanced requirement for regulated customers.

## Key Concepts

- Dynamic safety policy engine
- Prompt redaction and blocking
- API Management routing
- Grounding with versioned KB (Blob + Cognitive Search)
- Per-tenant isolation (Cosmos DB) and quotas
- Telemetry and auditing (Data Lake)

## Code Example

```javascript
// Minimal policy eval
function evaluatePrompt(prompt, policies) {
  for (const p of policies) {
    if (p.types?.some(t => prompt.includes(t))) {
      return {blocked: true, reason: p.reason}
    }
  }
  // simple redact example
  const redacted = prompt.replace(/SSN-\d{4}/g, '[REDACTED_SSN]')
  return {blocked: false, redacted}
}
```

